"# Wilde\nPart of my motivation for letting Lincoln take the car was I could instead draw a surprisingly gorgeous \\(even though it's fairly simple\\) fur coat olivia wilde wore as part of some photoshoot for a variety article that talks a little bit about a marvel project she's working on\\.\n\nIt was weird, reddit just blasted me with this thumbnail and I was like wait what what are you doing r/MarvelStudiosSpoilers?\n\nhttps://variety\\.com/2022/film/features/olivia\\-wilde\\-harry\\-styles\\-sex\\-scenes\\-dont\\-worry\\-darling\\-1235347929/\n\n---\n\nI was interrupted by mom coming home, but I think she's back downstairs now and I can finish this\n\nI want to leave the door open because I want to know when Lincoln comes home so I know my car is safe\\.\n\n---\n\n![](dayone-moment://E976E660425747A28B5C546DB8DA8647)\n\nI'll add color \\(what little there is\\) another day\n\n---\n\nAlso also\n\nThat coat, for starters, is definitely fake\n\nBut I looked it up\nAnd it's designer \\- \"Saint Laurent\"\n\nAnd despite being both fake and relatively simple in design, it is $15,600\\.\n\nMortimer: “you sure it’s fake?”\n\nYeah\n\nI was confident based on just the photos, and the listing itself calls it \"LONG COAT IN ANIMAL\\-FREE FUR\"\n\n\"animal\\-free\" feels like such a strange way to refer to it\n\nI mean I guess it's understandable from a quality perspective\n\nA lot of fake fur is cannolity, but this one, from a distance, looks very realistic\\. The shine of it, the way the light plays across it in that photo of her standing, looks authentic\\.\n\n---\n\nIt continues to weird me out how other, normal people just sort of don't pay attention to fur clothing, it's just a material like any other, something to casually notice in passing and that's all\\.\nAnd I\"m here just being hyperaware of everything\n\n---\n\nLincoln's home and all sounds well\\.\n\n---\n\nMortimer was talking about being sensitive to texture and thinking having a “sexual fascination with texture” \\(a really interesting lens to look at it through that I hadn’t thought of\\) might be stressful\\. \n\nAnd it occurred to me to ask her:\n\n> I'm gonna ask a stupid ass question\n> Because now it's in my head\n> I'm pretty sure I already know the answer, and it sounds especially silly out of context\n> But given how you've been discussing texture sensitivity\n> From that perspective\n> Does the idea of wearing fur or similar clothing sound unpleasant to you?\n\nAnd her response:\n\n> Hmmm\\. I don't THINK so? Like\\. My elephant blanket is really soft and nice\\. So I think fur would probably be soft and nice, except for when I have those hyper sensitive days where, like, everything hurts? Cause then furry things feel\\.\\.\\. like\\. Scratchy?"
